# The seed dataset is regenerated and compared byte for byte.
#
# `pnpm seed:generate` writes every file under seed/ with explicit `\n` line
# endings and no byte-order mark. Without the rules below, git on Windows would
# check the same bytes back out as CRLF and the determinism test would fail on
# one platform and pass on the other — the single most confusing way for this
# gate to break.
seed/** text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
